{"ref":"BDB, צַח²","hw":"צַח²","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">צַח</span></big>  <strong>adj. dazzling, glowing, clear</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">חֹם צַת</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 18:4\" href=\"/Isaiah.18.4\">Is 18:4</a> <em>glowing heat;</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">רוּחַ צַח</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 4:11\" href=\"/Jeremiah.4.11\">Je 4:11</a> <em>glowing wind;</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">דּוֹדִי צַח וְאָדוֹם</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 5:10\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.5.10\">Ct 5:10</a> <em>my beloved is dazzling</em> (<em>white</em>) <em>and ruddy</em> (cf. <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 4:7\" href=\"/Lamentations.4.7\">La 4:7</a>); fpl. <span dir=\"rtl\">לְדַבֵּר צַחוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 32:4\" href=\"/Isaiah.32.4\">Is 32:4</a> <em>to speak clear</em> (words), <em>clearly</em>.","next":"BDB, צָחִיחַ","prev":"BDB, צָחַח"}